    note node_filesystem_files and _files_free are 0 for CIFS: SMB does
    not report an inode budget, which is why the inode alert is scoped to
    the XFS mount only. Including CIFS would evaluate 100*(1-0/0) = NaN,
    a value that never crosses a threshold and looks healthy forever.

    SMB client health from /proc/fs/cifs, exported via the textfile
    collector. A share can be mounted, writable and reporting free space
    while the session reconnects on every operation - the filesystem
    collector cannot see that, and reconnects are the leading indicator.
